WEBVTT

00:00.140 --> 00:01.260
Welcome to Chapter 3.

00:01.560 --> 00:02.820
Well done on continuing.

00:03.120 --> 00:03.910
So far,

00:04.260 --> 00:05.790
we've talked about reading a graph,

00:06.090 --> 00:08.466
finding the key features and choosing

00:08.466 --> 00:10.780
precise words to describe the trends.

00:11.080 --> 00:12.032
That's progress.

00:12.032 --> 00:14.384
Now we're going to make sure your grammar

00:14.384 --> 00:15.560
is just as accurate,

00:15.560 --> 00:18.360
because grammar is a quarter of your Task 1 score.

00:18.660 --> 00:20.785
Let's start with the question

00:20.785 --> 00:23.760
students ask me the most: which tense? So,

00:24.060 --> 00:25.892
have a look at the graph.

00:25.892 --> 00:28.075
This graph shows electric cars

00:28.075 --> 00:30.400
as a percentage of new cars sold.

00:30.700 --> 00:31.730
Look at the line.

00:32.100 --> 00:35.195
It's solid up to 2024, then it becomes dashed.

00:35.195 --> 00:37.500
That tells you something important.

00:37.800 --> 00:40.627
The solid part has already happened,

00:40.627 --> 00:42.691
so we use the past simple.

00:42.691 --> 00:45.060
In 2015, electric cars made up

00:45.060 --> 00:46.970
just 1% of new car sales.

00:47.270 --> 00:50.720
The figure rose to 9% in 2021

00:50.720 --> 00:53.480
and reached 18% in 2024.

00:53.780 --> 00:55.897
The dashed part is a projection,

00:55.897 --> 00:59.040
so we switch to a future form for that part only.

00:59.340 --> 01:04.105
The figure is expected to reach 30% by 2027,

01:04.105 --> 01:08.340
and is projected to rise to 45% by 2030.

01:08.640 --> 01:11.015
You can add some grammatical range

01:11.015 --> 01:12.576
with the past perfect,

01:12.576 --> 01:15.290
but only with a clear point in the past.

01:15.590 --> 01:16.460
For example:

01:16.760 --> 01:20.980
“By 2021, the share had risen to 9%.”

01:21.280 --> 01:23.289
And here, the share of what?

01:23.289 --> 01:26.060
The share of new car sales, for example.

01:26.360 --> 01:28.040
So specify what

01:28.410 --> 01:30.390
it is that you're talking about as well.

01:30.690 --> 01:33.143
As an examiner, one of the most common

01:33.143 --> 01:35.408
mistakes I saw was the wrong tense.

01:35.408 --> 01:37.799
It's quite a serious mistake as well.

01:37.799 --> 01:39.308
It shows a basic error.

01:39.308 --> 01:41.573
Students would write something like

01:41.573 --> 01:44.152
“The number of electric cars is rising”,

01:44.152 --> 01:46.480
when the graph showed it in the past.

01:46.780 --> 01:47.571
It should be:

01:47.571 --> 01:49.550
“The number of electric cars rose.”

01:49.850 --> 01:51.859
Remember, the past of “rise” is “rose”,

01:51.859 --> 01:54.320
a bit like the flower, if it helps to remind you.

01:54.730 --> 01:57.528
So before you write, check the dates.

01:57.528 --> 02:00.988
If it's already happened, use the past simple.

02:00.988 --> 02:04.228
If it's a prediction, use “is expected to”,

02:04.228 --> 02:07.320
or “is projected to”, or “is forecast to”,

02:07.620 --> 02:08.766
and then the verb.

02:08.766 --> 02:11.360
Now have a go at the activity on the right.
